{
  "date": "2026-05-31",
  "period_start": "2026-05-01",
  "period_end": "2026-05-31",
  "title": "Video and audio grew up",
  "summary": "May widened the creative API stack—especially video, audio, and model choice—while making the surrounding tools easier for developers and contributors to use.\n\nVideo gained 120-second Nova Reel generations, Seedance 2.0, LTX-2 image-to-video, and start-to-end-frame transitions across the API, SDK, CLI, and MCP tools. Audio added fast ElevenLabs Flash speech, diarized transcription, AssemblyAI models, and an OpenAI-compatible realtime voice endpoint.\n\nThe text API added GPT-5.5, Gemma 4 26B, Gemini 3.5 Flash, Mistral 4, Claude Opus 4.8, Perplexity Sonar, StepFun, and more, alongside vision-capable Llamas and a dedicated embeddings endpoint for search, clustering, and RAG.\n\nDeveloper tooling became more practical: earnings visibility and BYOP attribution improved, docs gained LLM-ready copy controls and readable generated references, and official React and UI packages reduced OAuth and wallet setup to a few imports.\n\nRouting, validation, retries, caching, and upstream error handling received a long repair pass across image, video, text, and transcription. Long-running jobs got room to finish, while bad inputs increasingly return the actual reason instead of a ceremonial 500.",
  "pr_count": 226,
